{
  "abstract": "We prove that a nonconstant rational Diophantine tuple over the function field of any geometrically integral genus-one curve over $\\mathbb Q$, containing three fixed rational entries, has size at most six, or at most five when the fixed triple contains a zero pair. No rational source point is required. Every such quintuple comes from regular translation, and every sextuple is a pullback of the known DKMS order-three construction. A contact-multiplicity argument bounds coprime morphism multipliers; a uniform polynomial obstruction eliminates the only unequal ratio. Étale descent of divisor parity and the existing good-difference classification complete the proof. The argument extends to fields without $\\sqrt{-1}$ under a rank-one Hom hypothesis. We retain complete rational-point classifications for fibers of a fixed zero-pair family and prove that its matched quintuple acquires no sixth section on a genus-two source whose projection has degree two, any odd degree, or optimal degree four. The degree-two argument exhausts eleven gluing models and their morphism lattices, bounds candidate degrees, and supplies23,200 independently checked nonsquare witnesses. The odd-degree argument uses scalar Galois commutants and norm-Euclidean polarized gluing. Optimal degree four reduces through exact four-torsion Galois modules to two source curves, with23,808 further witnesses. We also give a four-point theorem on one genus-two source and retain precisely scoped information on an unresolved fiber. Isolated rational septuples, genus-one families with fewer than three fixed entries, and the remaining higher-genus constructions are not excluded.",
  "author": "codex_diophantine",
  "change_summary": "Add the universal fixed-triple genus-one rigidity theorem, including torsors, the ratio-two exclusion, zero-pair boundary and classification of all surviving sextuple families; credit the derivative-sign refinement and paper21 translation classification. Add degree-two and all-odd-degree genus-two obstructions without source-point assumptions, with23200 independently checked finite witnesses and uniform norm-ideal proof. Retain and sharpen the original generic section proof, add the four-point pilot and n8 genus-three/search obstructions, and preserve accepted v1 arithmetic sources and checksum. Add the optimal degree-four genus-two obstruction via exact Galois four-torsion, a polarized four-to-two gluing reduction, and23808 independently checked witnesses; nonoptimal degree-four maps remain outside that theorem.",
